{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use Java Config (Spring's annotation-based configuration) as the primary mechanism for defining custom job modules, while preserving backward compatibility with XML-based module definitions.",
    "Leverage the upstream Spring Batch fix to remove the XD-2486 workaround rather than re-implementing the decoupling in XD itself; this requires a Spring Batch version upgrade as a prerequisite.",
    "Design the cloud-platform SPI (U6) as a Java service-provider interface with a default Receptor implementation, isolating Lattice/Diego-specific logic behind the SPI so that alternative container runtimes can be plugged in later.",
    "Implement Hadoop namenode configuration via XD's standard serverside/clientside YAML configuration, using property names consistent with the existing spring.hadoop.config.* namespace.",
    "Implement the jdbchdfs passthrough mode as a new reader/processor/writer triplet wired by the job DSL, bypassing the chunk-oriented infrastructure of Spring Batch while still benefiting from the job lifecycle.",
    "Model the HDFS-resident Python script (U8) as an XD module option that stages the script to a local temp file at launch time and then delegates to the existing shell-processor mechanism, with stdin/stdout used for data exchange with the Python runtime.",
    "Store shortDescription as a new metadata key in the existing module YAML/properties descriptor and surface it through the module-info/admin REST endpoints and the documentation site generator.",
    "Migrate wiki content to AsciiDoc (consistent with the Spring documentation conventions) under a docs/ directory in the project repository and configure the build to publish it via the existing documentation site pipeline."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer performs all work; no team coordination overhead is included.",
    "The target codebase is Spring XD; the developer is already familiar with Spring Batch, Spring Integration, Spring Data, and the XD module/sparkline/job deployment model.",
    "The Spring Batch fix referenced by U4 is already available in a release that XD can upgrade to; only the upgrade integration and XD-2486 workaround removal are in scope.",
    "Wiki content is of moderate size (~50–100 pages); larger content would scale the U1 effort linearly.",
    "HDFS client libraries and the existing shell-processor infrastructure are already present; U8 is an extension, not a greenfield integration.",
    "Java 8 is the target language level (consistent with Spring XD 1.x at the time of these user stories), unless a later baseline is implicitly required.",
    "Unit tests are included inside each feature activity; the separate 'integration testing' activity covers cross-feature end-to-end and cluster-level tests only.",
    "Cloud-foundry Diego/Lattice and Receptor are available in the developer's environment for U6 spike work; no infrastructure provisioning is required.",
    "The existing CI pipeline (Gradle/Maven) is functional; the 'Build/CI configuration' activity covers only the deltas introduced by the new features (e.g., new modules, doc publishing).",
    "All effort estimates are in work-hours of focused development time and exclude meetings, waiting time, and unrelated overhead."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and technical design",
      "activity_description": "Review all eight user stories, reconcile dependencies (notably U4 depending on an upstream Spring Batch fix and U6 building on prior XD-on-Lattice work), draft an overall implementation plan, and produce short technical-design notes for the non-trivial items (U4, U6, U8).",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1: Migrate wiki content into the project repository",
      "activity_description": "Convert wiki pages to AsciiDoc under docs/, fix cross-links, tag content with module/code references, update the build to publish the docs, and remove wiki-only navigation and external wiki references from the codebase.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2: Hadoop namenode specifics in XD configuration",
      "activity_description": "Add namenode (fs.defaultFS / HDFS URI) properties to the XD config schema, wire them into Hadoop configuration bootstrap so a new DSL session picks them up automatically, and add tests for both single-node and HA namenode configurations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3: jdbchdfs batch job passthrough mode",
      "activity_description": "Introduce a passthrough option on the jdbchdfs job definition that bypasses Spring Batch's chunk-oriented read/process/write loop while preserving job lifecycle, error handling, and metrics. Implement, document, and test the new mode.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4: Decouple execution context from job launch lifecycle",
      "activity_description": "Upgrade the Spring Batch dependency to the release that contains the upstream fix, remove the XD-2486 workaround code paths, adapt XD's job-launcher to the new contract, and verify that classloader and serialization errors are no longer present under multi-tenant and redeployment scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5: Java Config support for custom job modules",
      "activity_description": "Reproduce the reported 'job does not exist' error for a Java-Config-based custom job module, fix the module-resolution/registration path so that @Configuration-based job modules are discovered, registered, and launched correctly, and add end-to-end tests covering the Java Config deployment flow.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6: Pluggable cloud-platform SPI for XD on Diego/Lattice",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement a generic ContainerRuntime SPI in XD that abstracts container instance lifecycle, health, and placement. Provide a Receptor-based implementation as the first concrete adapter, refactor existing Lattice-specific code to use the SPI, and validate with the XD-on-Lattice/Diego PoC.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7: Add shortDescription to module documentation",
      "activity_description": "Extend the module metadata schema to include shortDescription, update every existing job/stream/processor module's descriptor, expose the field through the admin/UI module listing, regenerate documentation, and add a validation test that fails CI when shortDescription is missing.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U8: Host/read Python script from HDFS for the shell processor",
      "activity_description": "Extend the shell processor to accept a hdfs:// script location on CF/XD, stage the script locally, invoke the Python interpreter, and pipe data to/from the Python process using the existing stdin/stdout protocol. Cover error handling, HDFS failures, and large-script scenarios with tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 28
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Integration and system testing",
      "activity_description": "Run cross-feature end-to-end tests in an XD cluster: namenode config + jdbchdfs passthrough (U2/U3), Spring Batch upgrade + custom Java-Config job (U4/U5), SPI-driven container lifecycle (U6), shortDescription in admin UI (U7), and HDFS-Python data-science loop (U8). Validate regression of the wiki-as-code doc build (U1).",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Build and CI configuration updates",
      "activity_description": "Update Gradle/Maven scripts and CI pipelines to publish the new AsciiDoc docs (U1), enforce shortDescription validation (U7), include the new Java-Config module test set (U5/U6), and add the HDFS-Python integration test (U8).",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Final documentation, code review, and refactoring",
      "activity_description": "Update user-facing reference docs and release notes for all features, address code-review comments, perform final cleanup/refactoring, and tag a release candidate.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 210
  }
}
